 to Japan's modernization efforts during the Meiji Restoration and remains a pivotal point in East Asian urban development. The city was designed under the guidance of American architect William Merrell Vories, incorporating Western planning principles which were rare in Japan's traditional cities. Sapporo’s development was symbolic of Japan's rapid industrialization and urbanization during the early 20th century, reflecting broader trends in modernization that influenced other cities across Asia.

